title: Radek in the Lobby
subtitle: Moscow's man has a proposal for every current.
view-if: congress_leipzig = 1 and congress_closing = 0 and e23_lz_radek_used = 0 and comintern_member = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.month_actions += 1;
Q.e23_lz_radek_used = 1;
RG.congress.tally();
Q.e23_lz_radek_name = (typeof Q.comintern_rep === 'string' && Q.comintern_rep) ? Q.comintern_rep : 'Karl Radek';
Q.e23_lz_with_moscow = (Q.moscow_backs == Q.congress_backing) ? 1 : 0;
Q.e23_lz_has_rival = Q.congress_rival ? 1 : 0;
Q.sys_outcome = 0;
!}
frequency: 150
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: congress

= Radek in the Lobby

[+ e23_lz_radek_name +] has spent the congress in the lobby, with a cigarette and a different joke for every delegation. In the evening he sends for the Zentrale's whips. The Executive, he says, wants a strong Zentrale and an unbroken party, and it will not mind very much who leads it as long as both sides are inside.

[? if e23_lz_with_moscow = 1 : The Executive is with our motion, he adds, and he would be glad to say so from the platform. ?][? if e23_lz_with_moscow = 0 : The Executive's sympathies, he admits, lie with the [+ moscow_backs_name +]. ?] [? if e23_lz_has_rival = 1 : What he offers is a compromise with the [+ congress_rival_name +]. ?]

- @compromise: Accept Radek's compromise: seats in the Zentrale for the [+ congress_rival_name +].
- @speak: Ask Radek to speak for our motion.
- @decline: Tell him the German party will settle this itself.

@compromise
subtitle: Their delegates vote with us, and they will share the Zentrale if we win. Moscow is pleased.
view-if: e23_lz_has_rival = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.e23_lz_deal_name = Q.congress_rival_name;
RG.congress.deal(Q.congress_rival);
RG.ecci('radek', 8);
RG.ecci('lenin', 3);
Q.independence -= 3;
Q.unity += 2;
!}

Two hours in a back room, a bottle of Saxon brandy and a list of names. The [+ e23_lz_deal_name +] withdraw their motion and will vote for ours.

@speak
subtitle: [? if lock_moscow_orders = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] If Moscow is with us, he can move the hall. If it is not, he will say so.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_moscow_orders == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 5;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 5;
}
if (Q.e23_lz_with_moscow == 1) {
    RG.congress.sway(0.08);
    Q.sys_outcome = 1;
} else {
    RG.congress.swayTo(Q.moscow_backs, 0.05);
    Q.sys_outcome = 2;
}
Q.independence -= 3;
RG.ecci('radek', 4);
!}

[? if sys_outcome = 1 : Radek speaks for forty minutes, in a German better than most of the delegates', and [+ congress_last_moved +] of them come over to us. ?][? if sys_outcome = 2 : Radek speaks for the Executive, which is to say for the [+ moscow_backs_name +], and [+ congress_last_moved +] delegates go over to them. We asked for it. ?]

@decline
subtitle: Independence grows, and the Spartacists approve. Radek takes it personally.
on-arrival: {!
Q.independence += 4;
RG.ecci('radek', -8);
RG.ecci('zinoviev', -3);
RG.congress.sway(0.02);
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction += 3;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
!}

We thank the Executive's representative for his advice. A few delegates who dislike being told what to do by Moscow come over to us for that reason alone. Radek's report to Zinoviev that night is two pages long.
